---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const APP_URL = "https://trading.onquantex.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security"
  description="How Quantex actually protects your account: trade-only API keys, manual withdrawal approval, an immutable ledger, and bots that fail safe."
>
  <section class="qx-sec-hero">
    <div class="qx-container">
      <span class="qx-eyebrow">Security</span>
      <h1>Security boundaries built in, not bolted on</h1>
      <p class="qx-lead">
        These are limits built into the system, not promises we're
        asking you to trust. Here's what each one actually does.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>The Binance keys can trade. They can't withdraw.</h2>
      <p>
        Every bot, and every spot trade, executes through Quantex's own
        Binance API keys. Those keys are generated with read and trade
        permissions only. Withdrawal permission is never granted on them:
        not disabled after the fact, never enabled in the first place.
        Even if those keys were somehow exposed, they physically couldn't
        move funds off Binance. Binance itself would refuse the
        request.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section qx-section-alt">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>Withdrawals need a human, every single time</h2>
      <p>
        Getting your identity verified doesn't put withdrawals on
        autopilot. Every withdrawal request, regardless of size, sits in a
        review queue and needs a manual approval before it's ever
        broadcast. There's no threshold under which it skips review, and
        no "trusted account" fast lane. The same check happens every
        time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Identity verification itself works the same way: submissions are
        reviewed by a person, not an automated pass/fail, and every
        decision (approved or rejected) is logged against who reviewed it
        and when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>Your balance is a history, not a number</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing about your balance lives as a single editable field
        somewhere. Every deposit, withdrawal, fee, and bonus is written
        as its own append-only ledger entry. Your balance is the sum of
        that history, not a value someone could quietly overwrite. If
        something ever looks wrong, there's a full trail to check it
        against, not just a number to take on faith.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section qx-section-alt">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>Bots fail safe, not silent</h2>
      <p>
        If a bot can't reach Binance, it doesn't sit there retrying
        forever, and it doesn't fail quietly either. After a handful of
        failed attempts in a row, it pauses itself automatically, and
        you're notified by email and browser push that it paused and why.
        A stuck connection turns into a bot doing nothing and telling you
        about it, not a bot doing something unexpected.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-cta">
    <div class="qx-container qx-cta-inner">
      <div>
        <h2>Ready to trade?</h2>
        <p>Create an account, deposit crypto, and put these limits to work for you.</p>
        <a class="qx-btn-primary qx-btn-lg" href={`${APP_URL}/signup`}>Trade Now</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .qx-sec-hero {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0 var(--space-24);
  }
  .qx-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-base);
    background: var(--teal-pale);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  .qx-sec-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px);
    color: var(--ink-base);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .qx-lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  .qx-section {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0;
  }
  .qx-section-alt {
    background: var(--cream-deep);
  }

  .qx-cta {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0 var(--space-32);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner {
    background: var(--teal-deep);
    border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
    padding: var(--space-48);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner h2 {
    color: var(--on-accent);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner p {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--teal-sage);
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner .qx-btn-primary {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .qx-container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-16);
    }
    .qx-sec-hero {
      padding: var(--space-32) 0 var(--space-16);
    }
    .qx-sec-hero h1 {
      font-size: 26px;
    }
    .qx-lead {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .qx-section {
      padding: var(--space-32) 0;
    }
    .qx-cta-inner {
      padding: var(--space-32) var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
